## PICO-8 font

The PICO-8 font is published by Lexaloffle Games under the Creative Commons
CC0 1.0 Universal public domain dedication. pico-editor derives a 1-bit glyph
atlas from that font for display. The checked-in atlas data is distributed
under CC0 as well; the rest of pico-editor remains MIT-licensed.

The glyph bitmaps in `internal/font/glyphs.txt` were extracted once from the
font records in the PICO-8 0.2.7 data file. They are checked in; the build never
reads a PICO-8 installation. The atlas is verified pixel-for-pixel against
PICO-8 0.2.7 screenshots (see `docs/spikes/M1-input.md`). It is not a generic
pixel font and is not rendered with runtime TrueType anti-aliasing.

The M6 input screenshots under `testdata/pico8/input/` are one-time capture
artifacts used to verify key tables. They are not part of the editor's runtime
data and are not redistributed as a font or cart asset.

